-### The level operand, settled
-
-`OPUS-CONTRA-FABLE-REWARD-LEVEL` disputed whether the formula reads the **recipient's** level or the
-**corpse's**. Every case in this suite gives them different levels — the recipient at `0x30`, the
-corpse at `0x10`, with different `+0x88` bytes — so the two readings cannot both match. The
-reconstruction reads the **corpse's**, through the dying unit's own `+0x698`, and agrees with the
-shipped bytes on all 265 lines.
-
-The control that reads the recipient's level instead does more than disagree: **it cannot run.** The
-recipient pointer is allowed to be NULL on paths where the corpse is not, so a formula reading
-`recipient[+0x1C2]` dereferences NULL where the original dereferences the corpse. The control
-failed on all 265 lines, the driver dying at the first such case.
