 # Experience and License Point award
 
-> Who gets EXP and LP when something dies, how much, and the status conditions that quietly
-> cut a character out of the payout entirely.
-
-**PARTIAL.** The eligibility gates are read at tier 1 and are exact. The payout arithmetic is
-read in outline — the terms and their order are visible, but not every operand is resolved.
-Do not treat the formula as complete.
-
-## 1. What the player sees
-
-Kill something, and the party gains EXP and LP. Two things a player may have noticed without
-being told:
-
-**EXP is shared.** The amount each character receives is divided by how many are eligible, so
-a smaller active party earns more each.
-
-**A character in certain disabling states earns nothing from that kill** — not reduced, *zero*.
-It is skipped before any arithmetic happens, and nothing on screen explains why.
-
-That second rule is the same condition that stops a character acting at all, which is why
-being disabled during a fight costs progression as well as participation.
