+## 4. Data structures and formulas
+
+Let `level = u8[subject.stats+0x1C2]`, `baseline = u8[subject.stats+0x88]`,
+`baseRow = ptr[subject+0xE70]`, and `perLevelRow = ptr[subject+0xE78]`.
+
+```text
+rawEXP = signed32((level - baseline) * u32[perLevelRow+0x34] + u32[baseRow+0x34])
+EXP = rawEXP                         in the designated branch
+EXP = signed_trunc(rawEXP / n)       in the shared branch, n > 0
+EXP = 0                             in the shared branch, n == 0
+rawLP = (level - baseline) * u8[perLevelRow+0x2F] + u8[baseRow+0x2F]
 ```
 
-**`Reward_ComputeLicensePointsForRecipient` carries the identical `0x80000003` gate** and the
-same foe check — verified independently in its own body.
-
-That mask is the one already documented on the action side: the field-record bit-15 system
-tests `(statusLayer0 | statusLayer1) & 0x80000003` to decide whether a unit may act. Two
-different subsystems, the same two-layer OR, the same three bits (0, 1 and 31).
-
-**So the states that stop you acting also stop you earning.** That is a single design rule
-expressed in two places, and it was found by noticing the same constant twice rather than by
-looking for it.
-
-The offsets differ between the two sites — `+0x64`/`+0x3C` here versus `+0x68`/`+0x78` in the
-BKBI documentation — so these are either different structures or different views of one. ~~That
-is **not** resolved; see §7.~~ **Resolved 2026-09-12 (FABLE): the same two words.** On the stats
-record ([the stats-record field map](../08-Combat-Formula/Battle-Stats-Record/the-battle-stats-record-field-map.md)) `+0x3C` and `+0x64` are the two `u32` **status words** the status write targets
-(presence = `+0x3C | +0x64`), while `+0x68` and `+0x78` are the 16-byte **effect layers** (the
-mutable status layer and the derived augment layer) the formula merge reads; the action gate on
-[the bit-15 page](../03-World-Area-Field/Field-Record-Table/field-record-bit15-action-permission.md) §4 ORs `+0x3C` and `+0x64` and ignores the layers, and so does this one
-(`002F90F7`–`002F90FD`: `mov eax, [rbx+0x64]; or eax, [rbx+0x3C]; test eax, 0x80000003`). The
-"BKBI `+0x68`/`+0x78`" contrast was a category slip: those are not status words.
